# Third-party notices

`aludam-fullplate`'s own code is MIT licensed (see `LICENSE`). The package
ships one small module (a re-export of `aludam`) and no third-party code of
its own.

It declares exactly one dependency, `aludam[neural]`, so the dependency,
model-weight and evaluation-data inventory lives in one place: the
`THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES` file inside the `aludam` distribution, where every row
was verified against a named source on 2026-10-04. This file exists so this
distribution carries a notice next to its own license; it adds no rows
because it declares no dependencies beyond `aludam` itself.

Model weights are never bundled with either distribution; `aludam fetch`
downloads them at runtime under their own licenses, listed in `aludam`'s
notices.

This is not legal advice.
